---
const audiences = [
  'Psychotherapists & counsellors',
  'Coaches & facilitators',
  'Body- & breathworkers',
  'Yoga & meditation teachers',
  'Voice & music professionals',
  'Teachers, carers & leaders',
];
---

<section class="mc-who">
  <div class="mc-who-inner">
    <div class="we-eyebrow" style="justify-content: center;">Who it's for</div>
    <h2 class="we-h2">People who <em>hold space</em> — by profession or by calling.</h2>
    <div class="mc-who-chips">
      {audiences.map((a) => <span class="mc-who-chip">{a}</span>)}
    </div>
    <p class="mc-who-note">
      And people quietly training toward this kind of work. Useful whether or
      not you ever intend to teach sounding formally — it begins with what it
      does in your own practice, and in you.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
